claude-wg-peer
==============

The package wraps the distribution-provided wg-quick@wg-claude.service. It does
not own the live /etc/wireguard/wg-claude.conf or either private key. Installation
does not enable, restart or modify the running tunnel.

The package-owned forward unit, nft policy and key-loading drop-in are installed
as static files. They become runtime state only after an owner explicitly runs
`claude-wg-peer adopt-existing --yes --restart` for an existing deployment, or
uses the explicit fresh-server sequence `init-server`, `register-peer` and a
separate service activation. There is no automatic failback or legacy runtime
path.

The files under /usr/lib/claude-wg-peer/ are non-secret package assets. Never
copy a historical no-peer server config over a live WireGuard config. Do not use
Cockpit's NetworkManager editor to manage this interface.

Before adoption, capture a verified backup of the live configuration on the VPS
under root-only permissions and coordinate maintenance with the WSL client
owner. Adoption requires the three original manual runtime files, checks the unit and
policy against the reviewed historical template SHA-256 values, verifies that
the drop-in matches the package, and removes only those exact matches after
live peer, address, SSH/route and nft checks. An unknown or partial legacy
runtime is rejected before any deletion or service restart. The read-only
`status`, `verify`, `check-firewall` and `check-peer` commands never print key
contents. Nothing in this package grants other VPS agents permission to modify
the protected peer.

Removal while a service is active is deliberately refused. dpkg can leave its
selection at "deinstall ok installed" after such a refusal; reinstall the
reviewed package version to restore "install ok installed" before further
package operations. Do not stop a live peer merely to satisfy package removal.
